From: Sakib Khan <sakikhan@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:13:44 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 12/13] feat(qti): add nord clock driver

Add the nord clock back-end: GCC clocks for the main, NE, NW and SE
domains, GPU/display GDSC sequencing and per-instance NSP/GPU/display
gating. Enable RPMh rail voting for nord and run the xPU static config
while the init clocks are held.

Hold the TZ votes for the SMMU TCU, GPU SMMU and PCIe SMMU clocks and
their vote GDS while the init clocks are on, so the secure SMMU
registers can be programmed, and release them in post-init. GPU
instances that chipinfo reports disabled are skipped.

Depends on the nord RPMh target support (rsc_regs.h and
rpmh_target.h), which is submitted separately.

Tested with: make PLAT=nord DEBUG=1 SPD=opteed bl31

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5 [claude-code]
